---
import ContactIcon from '../components/ContactIcon.astro';
import '../styles/utility-approved.css';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Privacy and site information" cta={false}>
 <article class="ut-reading ut-policy-layout rd-wrap rd-page">
 <header class="rd-pagehead"><h1>Privacy and site information</h1><p>How inquiry drafts are stored and how to use the product information on this site.</p></header>
 <div class="ut-policy-columns"><nav class="ut-toc" aria-label="Privacy topics"><a href="#your-inquiry">Your inquiry</a><a href="#saved-drafts">Saved drafts</a><a href="#external-services">External services</a><a href="#site-information">Site information</a><a href="#privacy-contact">Contact</a></nav><div class="ut-policy-body">
 <section id="your-inquiry" data-core-section="your-inquiry"><h2>Your inquiry</h2><p>The <a href="/quote/">inquiry form</a> creates an email draft in your browser. It does not send your information to LZZ or upload drawings. To contact us, open the draft in your email app, add your attachments and send it yourself.</p><figure class="ut-policy-image" data-image-origin="original-ui-screenshot"><picture><source media="(max-width:767px)" srcset="/media/image-led-20261015/privacy-draft-mobile.webp"/><img src="/media/image-led-20261015/privacy-draft.webp" width="1520" height="102" alt="Screenshot of the draft controls: Open email app, Edit details, Copy draft and Save draft"/></picture><figcaption>Screenshot of the inquiry form. Opening your email app is separate from sending.</figcaption></figure></section>
 <section id="saved-drafts" data-core-section="saved-drafts"><h2>Saved drafts</h2><p>Your input is kept in this browser tab so you can continue after a refresh. The draft is associated with the part or topic used when you entered the form. </p><p>Changing the product or service inside the form updates that same draft; it does not create a separate saved copy. These details are not sent to LZZ or saved to an account.</p><p>Select “Clear saved input” to remove the draft for the current entry context, including older copies associated with that entry. A browser that restores an earlier session may also restore your draft. Clear your input when using a shared device.</p><figure class="ut-policy-image" data-image-origin="original-ui-screenshot"><picture><source media="(max-width:767px)" srcset="/media/image-led-20261015/privacy-clear-mobile.webp"/><img src="/media/image-led-20261015/privacy-clear.webp" width="1520" height="90" alt="Screenshot of the saved-draft status and Clear saved input button" loading="lazy"/></picture><figcaption>Screenshot of the saved-input control. Use it in the inquiry form.</figcaption></figure><p>If storage is blocked or full, you can still prepare a draft while the page is open, then choose “Save draft” to keep a text copy.</p></section>
 <section id="external-services" data-core-section="external-services"><h2>Cookies and external services</h2><p>This site does not use analytics or advertising cookies. Your email provider, WhatsApp and other linked websites have their own privacy policies.</p></section>
 <section id="site-information" data-core-section="site-information"><h2>Product and company information</h2><p>Product pages describe example parts and the information needed to quote a similar component. They are not independently verified specifications for the pictured parts. Your drawing and quotation define the material and tolerances, with inspection and commercial terms confirmed for your order. Original catalog records are retained in our archive.</p><p>The engineering guides help you prepare an inquiry. They contain no customer inspection results and do not establish suitability for a particular application. English summaries explain the <a href="/about/company-profile/#documents">company documents</a>; contact LZZ to verify their current validity. <a href="/factory/#quality">Inspection planning</a> is agreed for your order.</p><figure class="ut-policy-image ut-policy-image--part" data-image-origin="source-listing"><img src="/media/product-sources-20261015/p02-800.webp" width="800" height="800" alt="Original machined impeller reference photograph showing visible shape, not verified dimensions" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>A reference photograph shows visible form. The drawing and agreed records define the order.</figcaption></figure></section>
 <section id="privacy-contact" data-core-section="privacy-contact"><h2>Contact</h2><p>Hangzhou Lizhizao Precision Machinery Co., Ltd. For questions about this site, contact <a class="contact-link" href="mailto:roger@lzz-cnc.com"><ContactIcon kind="email"/><span>roger@lzz-cnc.com</span></a></p><p class="ut-revision">Updated 16 October 2026.</p></section>
 </div></div></article>
</Layout>

